      "text": "1. Added to both files to accomplish the requirements of the LaTeX problem format.\n\nIn right triangle $SQP$, $\\tan R = \\frac{QP}{QR}$.\n\n2. In right triangle $SQR$, $\\tan R = \\frac{QS}{QH}$.\n\n3. Since the triangles are similar, the ratios of their corresponding sides are equal, so $\\frac{QP}{QS} = \\frac{QR}{QH}$.\n\n4. Simplifying this ratio and using the given $\\cos R = \\frac{4}{9}$ and $\\sin R = \\frac{5}{9}$, we can find $QS$.\n$1.\\text{ }\\frac{QP}{QS}= \\frac{QR}{QH}$, which implies $\\frac{QS}{QP}=\\frac{QH}{QR}$.\n\n2.\\[\\frac{QS}{QP}=\\frac{QS}{9}=\\frac{QH}{QH+9}=\\frac{QP}{QP+QH}\\] Taking the reciprocal, $QS=QP\\frac{QH+9}{QM}$.\n\n3.\\$\\frac{QP}{QS}=\\frac{4}{9}=\\frac{QH}{\\frac{QH}{\\frac{4}{9}} + 9}= \\frac{QH}{QH+9} \\$\n\n4.\\[QS = 3\\frac{36}{36+36}=QS=3 \\cdot \\frac{9}{4} = \\textbf{9/4=2.25} \\$\n\nSo the final answer is clean number $2.25$.\n\n$ \\textbf{(C)}$ $\\text{9/4}$",
